# What NOT to publish to npm.
#
# This exists instead of a package.json "files" allowlist because vsce refuses
# to run when a .vscodeignore and "files" are both present ("VSCE does not
# support combining both strategies"), and .vscodeignore has to stay — it is
# what re-includes node_modules/tw-sugarcube-analyzer into the .vsix.
#
# So the two packagers are kept apart: vsce reads .vscodeignore, npm reads this.
# npm prefers .npmignore over .gitignore, so everything the .gitignore covered
# has to be repeated here.
#
# What ships: bin/, ts-plugin/, extension.js, passages.js, README.md, LICENSE,
# package.json. Check with `npm pack --dry-run` after changing anything.
.claude/
.git/
.gitignore
.npmignore
.vscodeignore
scripts/
test/
docs/
*.vsix
*.tgz
*.log
